<p>I'm actually a big fan of Scranton Reality Anchors, because some skips make no sense without them. If you've got something that can, say, teleport unlimited distances or rewind time, there's no variant of &quot;put it in a box with thick walls&quot; that seems at all believable. And as fun as they are in moderation, I would really prefer we don't require ancient Kabbalistic rituals or friendly Class 9999 reality warpers restraining all skips of this caliber.</p>
<p>Also, &quot;Reality Anchor&quot; gives a pretty decent idea of what the device does in general.</p>

